From d2c31b4f5c1360111c406ad36ec6fb9ca1164228 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kaivalyamahajan009-code
 <307739818+kaivalyamahajan009-code@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:16:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): render inline svg diagrams and fix latex
 delimiters

SVG diagrams
- Fenced ```svg blocks in assistant messages render as inline diagrams.
- While the fence is still streaming, a loading card shows the opencode
  progress indicator next to the diagram's <title>.
- Diagrams are shown through <img>, so scripts and remote resources never
  run; event handlers, <script>, foreignObject and unsafe hrefs are also
  stripped from the source. Invalid SVG falls back to the code.
- When OPENCODE_CLIENT=desktop, the system prompt tells the model it may
  answer with ```svg diagrams.

LaTeX
- Support \[ ... \] display math, including mid-sentence, instead of
  letting marked's escape rule turn it into literal brackets.
- Allow \( ... \) to wrap across lines and $$ ... $$ on a single line.
- Math never spans a blank line, so an unclosed delimiter can't swallow
  the rest of a streaming response.
- The streaming block splitter now uses the same block-math rules, so
  display math containing lines like "+ &" or "- &" is no longer torn
  apart into list items.
